        "id": 265747,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-06-30T18:13:10.783Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We’re off to a baneful start…</p>\n<p>“She’s like a magic lady at this point…” Oh, so it’s Madam Mittermaier.  That’s the villain of the story we don’t get this week.</p>\n<p>They definitely need to sell Sentinels Mad Libs.  They would make so much more money from that instead of a card game.</p>\n<p>I’m amazed that they listed off all the princesses, and didn’t get to Unity until 11.  (Also I’m now mad that Painstake wasn’t on the cover.)</p>\n<p>You absolutely do go punch Grimm out, that’s exactly how you win against his DE deck (which for now is his only deck).  He’s a single target villain, he can win without damaging you, but you absolutely cannot win without damaging him.</p>\n<p>Oh no, bear of burden with us!</p>\n<p>Battle On The Fourth Wall would be a great name for a Guise vs Grimm story.</p>",
